{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1096697-creating-a-pied-piper-changeling","id":1096697,"title":"Creating a Pied Piper Changeling","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Changeling: The Dreaming"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-05-25T06:30:36-07:00","id":1096697,"title":"Creating a Pied Piper Changeling","content":"I'm trying to make a Changeling adventure with a Pied Piper-like NPC that lures children in order to drain them of their Glamour. So I'm still thinking what kind of changeling kith would be apropiate. Obviously he is from the Unseelie court. I would go for Sidhe, but still have doubts. Also, what kind of Atributes and Skill distribution would be the more apropiate? Is there any character like that in the oficial books?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13478-drakeepsilon","name":"DrakeEpsilon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13478_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"43"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-25T07:57:27-07:00","id":1096715,"title":"","content":"The Gift of Pan would allow the character to play music and lower the inhibitions of his listeners, making it easier to lure them into following him. I would invest in high Charisma, Manipulation, and Expression.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13420-gl1tterboots","name":"gl1tterboots","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"58"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-25T08:23:32-07:00","id":1096731,"title":"","content":"Leanhaun Sidhe would be appropriate, but you do have plenty of choises where to take it depending on how Dark is your adventure.<br /> <br /> Unseelie Satyr would be another good choice with their musical talents and their birthright could bring a bit more bite to their music. Unless of course you want to use something else than enchanted music as a lure, but satyrs tend to be good at enticing in any case.<br /> <br /> Speaking of other lures... an Unseelie Boggan could lure kids to him with enchanted candy.<br /> <br /> A Nocker could use toys, as could the Boggan, though due to Nockers general demeanor luring kids could be harder for them, unless using magic to do the luring or using a basilisk stone before getting to it.<br /> <br /> Pooka are natural tricksters, and liars, so such luring is easy for them especially since they could use their animal forms, kids love cuddly animals, and/or their natural aptitude to get people talking to make the kids feel at home.<br /> <br /> Redcaps would be a good albeit a rather dark option. Especially if using magic to act as the actual lure as they might just decide to get rid of the kids after draining their Glamour in the way that is most natural to them. Think about it. No evidence left behind, no banal kid left to grow into a dangerously banal adult and you get a meal on top f it all, after all you are always hungry.<br /> <br /> Sluagh are another dark option, though they are more likely than the reds to leave the kids alive but likely suffering from nyktophobia and possibly aracnophobia as well.<br /> <br /> Of course any of the above could decide to kill the kids after ripping their Glamour if that is something you want to deal with in your chronicle. And like said pretty much any Kith could be used as a Pied Piper and if you want an especially dark chronicle same goes for Thallain as well.<br /> <br /> As for attributes and skills it does wholly depend on your choice of lure. If you want a literal piper Performance and Charisma would be good choices for example. If using a Nocker that lures kids with enchanted toys crafting would be the appropriate ability etc. <br /> <br /> Dont know if any of this is even useful to you but hopefully it has some ideas that you could put to use.<br /> <br /> If you want more specific help, or ideas thrown about, do elaborate further on your idea. Is it a literal piper? Do you intend for the children to survive? Or be oherwise unharmed and merely drained of their Glamour ? Etc.<br /> <br /> I'm happy to throw out ideas depending on what exactly you want/need.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1629-possessed","name":"Possessed","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1629_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1140"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-25T08:23:42-07:00","id":1096732,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13420-gl1tterboots\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar13420_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"13420\" data-vbnamecard=\"13420\">gl1tterboots</a> suggestion works. (Edit to add: As does <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1629-possessed\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1629_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1629\" data-vbnamecard=\"1629\">Possessed</a> ) The morganed's Song of the Sea could also work. Some Actor and Scene paired with some Summer, Sovereign, or Chicanery using a musical bunk could also get what you're after.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Charlie Cantrell</b><br /> Onyx Path Freelancer <hr />Changeling: The Dreaming 20th Anniversary Edition, Conquering Heroes, Book of Freeholds, Guide to the Night, C20 Players Guide","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/648-pookaknight","name":"PookaKnight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar648_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"690"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-25T08:50:30-07:00","id":1096746,"title":"","content":"I had a Bogie doing just that in my Chronicle, once. He didn't use special magic, only natural cunning and charm. But tracking the Bogie down was a real pain.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>...","edited":{"userid":5211,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5211-firkraag","user":"Firkraag","date":". 05-25-2017, 11:53 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5211-firkraag","name":"Firkraag","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5211_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"381"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-25T09:35:07-07:00","id":1096774,"title":"","content":"Well, yeah, I was thinking on a literal Piper, perhaps with a chimerical flute or something to the same effect, perhaps it would work so only children (and perhaps some childish adults) could hear the music. Also I don't think the children would die... at least at the beginning... Still planning the bases but what you have suggested sounds promising.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13478-drakeepsilon","name":"DrakeEpsilon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13478_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"43"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-25T11:21:03-07:00","id":1096799,"title":"","content":"I think that using the imbued treasure rules to imbue Summer 3 into a pipe could maybe do this. Make people really desire the music when played, so as long as you keep playing they'll do their best to stay in earshot?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13395-daniel-knight","name":"Daniel Knight","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"96"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-25T11:54:28-07:00","id":1096807,"title":"","content":"I have many problems with the Kith system in Changeling. I think the splat descriptions are overly narrow and specific which results in them having to keep adding a ridiculous # of kiths. I use much more general descriptions of kiths. As a result, I use 'Eshu&quot; for any kind of fairy creature that appears human, but which isn't part of any kind of nobility (like the sidhe). Therefore, that captures any kind of &quot;hero helpers&quot; fairy tale characters or human-like villainous helpers to fairytale monsters. Since the pied piper originally arrived to help the town, he fits the traditional &quot;hero helper&quot; model. It was only when the town reneged on his payment did he take their children away. So it fits the eshu model (at least in my schema).<br /> <br /> If you don't want a direct copy of the pied piper, but just want ideas for kiths that could be used as child snatchers, then it's pretty much your imagination. Possessed gave a lot of good ideas.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-25T13:28:09-07:00","id":1096844,"title":"","content":"I like to think of the Pied Piper as a Seelie Piskey. <br /> In his own eyes he is not &quot;Kidnapping&quot; the children, but saving them from their Banal parents.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10198-luisarmander","name":"Luisarmander","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"59"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-25T13:30:11-07:00","id":1096845,"title":"","content":"Spriggan with Contract arts and a Treasure Pipe? If contract is violated, which he now half encourages he uses Sovereign or chicanery or something to summon the children.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-26T06:49:26-07:00","id":1097105,"title":"","content":"You know, with all these suggestions I think I'll better do an entire group of unseelie changelings with the Pied Piper modus operanti of kidnapping children. It would be fun to have the group trying to descifer why some stories of the surviving children don't correlate.<br /> <br /> Thank you all!<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13478-drakeepsilon","name":"DrakeEpsilon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13478_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"43"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-26T14:07:43-07:00","id":1097285,"title":"","content":"Sounds fun.<br /> <br /> If you include my treasure example, then it goes without saying that the one who imbued the treasure is also part of this group and is handing out imbued pipes to any member with no other way to lure targets.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13395-daniel-knight","name":"Daniel Knight","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"96"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-26T22:18:33-07:00","id":1097423,"title":"","content":"One way to take this, if using enchanted pipes, could be that each piper is an independed, and likely even unaware of the others atleast initially, connected only by the mysterious benefactor who makes and distributes the pipes, or flutes or whatevers. It could be a Nocker or since the pipes seem to be masspriduced even a Boggan, and his/her motivations could be either sinister or bening. It could be that the changeling tries to help others of it's kind to gather Glamour and could be terrified to hear how the treasures are being used to harm the children or that could all be by it's design.<br /> <br /> In anycase I hope you all the best with your chronicle and hope we have provided you with some inspiration.<br /> <br /> And naturally incase it needs to be said the crafter who creates the pipes could be of any kith Or if of the more sinister type Thallain, or even another Gallain or Prodigal if you wish though if the latter it might not even realize all the consequences of it's actions regarding the Dreaming.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1629-possessed","name":"Possessed","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1629_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1140"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}